<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Society of United Irishmen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1791">1791</a>–<a href="/years/1798">1798</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as United Irishmen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Society of United Irishmen was founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belfast">Belfast</a> in 1791 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theobald-wolfe-tone">Theobald Wolfe Tone</a> and others, at first to seek parliamentary reform and Catholic emancipation. Inspired by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a> and suppressed by the government, it became a secret revolutionary movement seeking an Irish republic with French help. Its rebellion of 1798 was crushed and led directly to the Acts of Union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/society-of-united-irishmen.jpg" alt="Society of United Irishmen" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This vector image includes elements that have been taken or adapted from this file · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badge_of_the_Society_of_United_Irishmen_(coloured).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
